      "body": "## Problem\n\nThe previous original-kernel diagnostic reached the GENI HS protocol read at physical `0x00998068` and stopped with a kernel failure. This change adds a separately enabled reference profile for that next device boundary. Android userspace and UI have not been reached.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add default-off `qcom-sm8250-geni-hs` with strict 32-bit MMIO, bounded fixed-format FIFO state, independent serial backend, three GCC clock inputs, wrapper reset and sysbus IRQ.\n- Preserve the legacy UART's VMState and introduce a separate guard-first HS section. Reject invalid identity, register, FIFO, boolean, format and clock-witness state before backend activity.\n- Pin 19 public source inputs and two reviewed reference inputs, regenerate the 12 constants, and retain 49 pure source tests plus 51 source-generation negative cases.\n- Add the 55-group compiled-model contract, including two completed migrations, 30 complete stream files, 25 one-bit mutations, three structural mutations, two pure 49-getter observations and 58 required cleanup records.\n- Add an optional private job-local cache for complete immutable public sources. Each caller still verifies full source identities. Atomic no-replace publication preserves conflicting or incomplete entries.\n- Preserve all previous 104 normalized CI contracts and their order; the plan now contains 102 component gates and five Linux gates.\n\n## Validation and limits\n\nCurrent source: `70b387fb064cdf2099e85dd89213a5ea7e2c398f`  \nTree: `37bf696bc687422eac2bd967abda7d80af8e02b9`\n\nThe latest correction changes only the LLCC verifier's default input selection. It includes the complete, already-pinned upstream geometry source with its original BSD-3-Clause notice and full license. All eight complete inputs still pass the original length, SHA-256 and Git blob checks before regeneration. The other seven source paths and explicit `--source-root` mode are unchanged; missing or altered bundled bytes fail without a network fallback.\n\nOne full local LLCC regeneration passed with eight verified inputs and two outputs byte-identical to the existing C include and register manifest. Two bounded branch checks passed: the valid bundled input reaches the generator boundary after complete identity verification, and a one-bit change is rejected before generation. The branch checks make no network requests and deliberately do not execute the generator. All eleven published files were fully read back; their byte counts, SHA-256 and Git blob identities match. Eight changed Git trees and the exact single parent were also verified.\n\nBoth preceding e42 first-attempt workflows passed 101/102 components. Their sole failure was the eighth LLCC source download, which exhausted three HTTP 429 requests after 10s and 20s waits. Both A77 jobs succeeded, while later Linux gates were skipped. The corrected GENI source gate and all 55 compiled checks passed in both archives, including two migrations, 30 stream files and 58 cleanup records. These are component observations from failed overall workflows; independent complete migration-stream review and new-head qualification remain pending.\n\nThe earlier B5 cache/QOM failures, 4710 GENI/source-download failures and three bounded component-diagnostic failures remain preserved. Failed workflows have not been rerun or used for another original-kernel diagnostic. Downloader host tests remain 52, GENI source tests remain 49, and the previous 104 normalized contracts and order remain unchanged.\n\nThe current head also merges the target branch's two independently published storage-retirement metadata files. The exact two-parent merge adds only those documents to the corrected source; all executable source bytes remain unchanged. Its source tree and the current PR merge tree are identical.\n\nNatural CI has started for this head: [push run 45599002342](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/actions/runs/45599002342) and [PR run 45599016290](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/actions/runs/45599016290), both attempt 1. Qualification and the next original-kernel diagnostic require successful completion and full artifact review.\n\nThe device implementation, generated constants, 102+5 CI plan, harness, workflow, original boot inputs and five native runners are unchanged. The profile remains a reference implementation without firmware execution, DMA transfers, a Bluetooth peer or measured physical SE6 state. IRQ fixtures observe the actual device output without establishing GIC routing. Android userspace, UI and boot-complete have not been reached.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [Acceptance boundary](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/blob/b5bf00086640cbee8ef0c13375ba281cd73b8369/tb371fc/docs/geni-hs-sm8250-acceptance.md)\n- [Pinned source provenance](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/blob/b5bf00086640cbee8ef0c13375ba281cd73b8369/tb371fc/docs/geni-hs-sm8250.md)\n- [Source publication manifest](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/blob/b5bf00086640cbee8ef0c13375ba281cd73b8369/tb371fc/evidence/geni-hs-sm8250-20261125-6a5/source-publication-freeze.json)\n\n- [B5 failure and corrective publication](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/tree/4710b80bde965798dfe5f0c9684c5b5880b84d04/tb371fc/evidence/geni-hs-b5-ci-corrections-20261125-6a5)\n\n- [4710 failures, corrections and the passing component diagnostic](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/tree/e42c0a5934d36a1dc31de4ba30275672a919665a/tb371fc/evidence/geni-hs-4710-ci-corrections-20261125-6a5)\n\n- [e42 LLCC failures, fixed public input and local validation](https://github.com/cyjin-yl/qemu-tb371fc/tree/9e5dddcd0e0ba228821e733a7cf853bbd57dfd7b/tb371fc/evidence/llcc-bundled-geometry-e42-20261125-6a5)\n",
